---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  wide
  title="About"
  description="Ian Helfrich is a PhD economist, award-winning educator, applied researcher, and builder of open quantitative teaching tools based in St. Louis, Missouri."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Economist · Educator · Builder</span>
    <h1>I make difficult quantitative ideas usable.</h1>
    <p class="kicker">
      I am Ian Helfrich, a Georgia Tech–trained economist and educator based in St. Louis. My work moves between private teaching, applied economic research, and the tools that make both of those activities better.
    </p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button" href="/work-with-me">Work with me</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/cv">View my CV</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="positioning-statement">
    <div>
      <span class="section-label">The through-line</span>
      <h2>Structure first. Then technique.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="statement-copy">
      <p>
        Whether I am teaching an econometrics student, designing an empirical strategy, or building a research tool, I am usually solving the same problem: turning a complicated system into a structure someone can inspect, test, and use.
      </p>
      <p>
        My doctoral training is in international trade, networks, spatial heterogeneity, and optimal transport. My applied work spans labor and AI, place-based policy, causal inference, geospatial measurement, and quantitative research infrastructure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="modes-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">One practice, three modes</span>
        <h2 id="modes-title">Teaching, research, and construction.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Each mode disciplines the others: research keeps the teaching honest; teaching exposes weak explanations; building turns recurring needs into durable tools.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="method-grid">
      <article class="method-card">
        <h3>Teaching</h3>
        <p>More than 1,200 hours in a recent teaching year, 450+ students, a 5.0 average across 175+ public ratings, and Georgia Tech's 2023 Graduate Teaching Assistant of the Year award.</p>
        <a class="card-arrow" href="/teaching">Teaching record →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="method-card">
        <h3>Research</h3>
        <p>Active work in labor and AI, international trade, spatial and policy econometrics, networks, place-based investment, and quantitative measurement.</p>
        <a class="card-arrow" href="/research">Research program →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="method-card">
        <h3>Tools</h3>
        <p>Open instructional sites, empirical viewers, datasets, research pipelines, and computational infrastructure in Python, R, Stata, Julia, Go, and modern web tools.</p>
        <a class="card-arrow" href="/projects">Projects and tools →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="education-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">Training</span>
        <h2 id="education-title">An unusually interdisciplinary economics education.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Economics is the core, with serious training in geographic information science, public policy, networks, and quantitative methods.</p>
    </div>

    <ul class="credential-list">
      <li><strong>PhD, Economics</strong><br />Georgia Institute of Technology, 2024</li>
      <li><strong>MS, Geographic Information Science & Technology</strong><br />Georgia Institute of Technology, 2022</li>
      <li><strong>MS, Economics</strong><br />Georgia Institute of Technology, 2019</li>
      <li><strong>MA, Economics</strong><br />Indiana University Bloomington, 2018</li>
      <li><strong>MSc, Economics & Public Policy</strong><br />Barcelona School of Economics, 2015</li>
      <li><strong>BA, Economics</strong><br />University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, 2014</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="ethics-panel" aria-labelledby="teaching-title">
    <div>
      <span class="section-label">Why teaching remains central</span>
      <h2 id="teaching-title">Explanation is a form of analysis.</h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>I have taught or supported instruction at Georgia Tech, Duke University, Indiana University, and online degree programs, from principles courses through graduate econometrics and engineering signal processing.</p>
      <p><strong>A good explanation is not a simplified version of expertise. It is one of the strongest tests of it.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section compact" aria-labelledby="selected-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">Selected recognition</span>
        <h2 id="selected-title">Awards and service.</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Graduate Teaching Assistant of the Year</strong>, Georgia Institute of Technology, 2023.</li>
      <li><strong>Senator of the Year</strong>, Georgia Tech Graduate Student Government, 2020.</li>
      <li><strong>Graduate Teaching Fellow</strong>, Georgia Tech Center for Teaching and Learning, inaugural cohort.</li>
      <li><strong>Referee</strong>, <em>Journal of Economic Theory</em>, 2025.</li>
      <li><strong>Public Policy Thesis Competition finalist</strong>, Barcelona School of Economics, 2015.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section compact" aria-labelledby="outside-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">Beyond economics</span>
        <h2 id="outside-title">A teacher in more than one room.</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>
      I am also a third-degree black belt and longtime instructor in Sin Moo HapKiDo. That practice shaped much of how I think about instruction: demonstrate precisely, decompose movement, protect the learner while they fail, and gradually transfer control.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-panel">
    <span class="section-label">St. Louis · Working worldwide</span>
    <h2>Have a methods problem worth thinking through?</h2>
    <p>Private coaching, institutional teaching, research collaboration, and speaking inquiries each have a clear route.</p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button" href="/contact">Choose the right contact path</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
